"The prognosis is influenced by several factors, including a preoperative PSA of 7.8 and an ISUP grade group 3 (Gleason 4+3) identified on the prostatectomy specimen. Positive surgical margins are concerning findings. Countervailing points include no documented extraprostatic extension, absence of seminal vesicle invasion, and lack of lymphovascular invasion or node metastasis reported in the pathology. A notable discrepancy exists between the biopsy finding (ISUP grade group 2) and the prostatectomy result (ISUP grade group 3). The nodal status was assessed, with no metastasis noted. Missing postoperative PSA data prevents a full assessment of biochemical recurrence risk trajectory. Future prognosis revision would depend significantly on subsequent postoperative PSA levels and their pattern over time. The fixed estimated horizon is 56.82 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 42.61–71.02 months; its coverage has not been validated."
